      "url": "https://www.last.fm/music/Supergrass/I+Should+Coco",
      "wiki_content": "I Should Coco is the debut studio album by Supergrass, released through Parlophone in May 1995.\nThey released their debut single from the album, \"Caught by the Fuzz\", in May 1995 on the small independent local label Backbeat Records and was re-released with Parlophone.\nI Should Coco was recorded in Cornwall and produced by Sam Williams.\n\nAt the height of the Britpop era, the album became the band's most successful release when it reached number one on the UK Albums Chart, and subsequently gained platinum status for sales of album, which reached over a million copies worldwide and 500,000 in the UK.\n\nTitle:\nThe title of the album is cockney rhyming slang for \"I should think so''. (Rhyming slang is a form of phrase construction in the English language).\n\nCover art: \nThe front cover of the album is a painting based on three separate photos of Coombes, Goffey, and Quinn. The portraits of Coombes and Goffey were taken by Quinn in the summer of 1994 when he was experimenting with a macro lens. The photo of Quinn was taken that same year by a friend, while they were on tour in Wolverhampton. The painting was then created by the Moody Painters. <a href=\"https://www.last.fm/music/Supergrass/I+Should+Coco\">Read more on Last.fm</a>. User-contributed text is available under the Creative Commons By-SA License; additional terms may apply.",
      "wiki_summary": "I Should Coco is the debut studio album by Supergrass, released through Parlophone in May 1995. They released their debut single from the album, \"Caught by the Fuzz\", in May 1995 on the small independent local label Backbeat Records and was re-released with Parlophone. I Should Coco was recorded in Cornwall and produced by Sam Williams. At the height of the Britpop era, the album became the band's most successful release when it reached number one on the UK Albums Chart, and subsequently gained platinum status for sales of album, which reached over a million copies worldwide and 500,000 in <a href=\"https://www.last.fm/music/Supergrass/I+Should+Coco\">Read more on Last.fm</a>."
    },
    "perplexity": {
      "description": "I Should Coco is the debut album by Supergrass, released in 1995 on Parlophone, and it captures the band at full tilt: fast, cheeky, and overflowing with teenage energy. Built from a punchy blend of Britpop, punk rock, alternative rock, and pop-punk, the record is driven by sharp hooks, scrappy rhythms, and a sense of exuberant youth that became central to the band’s identity.\n\nThe album’s breakthrough came with “Alright,” a massively catchy single that turned Supergrass into one of the defining names of the Britpop era and helped send the album to No. 1 in the UK. Critics and listeners alike have long treated it as a landmark 1990s debut, praised for its immediacy, personality, and hit-packed momentum; its success also made it Supergrass’s most celebrated and commercially successful release.",
